# Procedural SDF Generator (Sanitized Backup)

This document retains a high-level description of the signed distance field generator without exposing restricted kernels or datasets.

## Core Responsibilities
- Accept path descriptions composed of lines and curves, normalize them, and emit textures consumable by the renderer.
- Provide helper utilities for common shapes so systems avoid duplicating geometry setup.
- Sampling kernels, acceleration structures, and fidelity heuristics are [REDACTED].

## Rendering Workflow
- Generated textures integrate with renderer-managed batching and smoothing controls.
- Anti-aliasing multipliers follow renderer fidelity hints to preserve crisp silhouettes across devices.
- Shader bindings, gradient tricks, and GPU resource policies are [REDACTED].

## Usage Pattern
- Systems request a path, run the generator at the desired resolution, and submit the resulting texture within their render pass.
- Concrete API signatures, platform-specific integrations, and diagnostic tooling are [REDACTED].
